{#
    One card, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property.** The directive says what the card is: the
    title, where it goes, the kind, the label, the picture. Each of those
    lands on `sds-card` as an attribute. Nothing here says what a card looks
    like: not the frame, not the row above the title, not what wraps a title.
    That is the whole point of a component.

    A template that spells `.sds-card__body` and `.sds-card__title` makes
    every internal name public API. It leaves the element to frame markup this
    file already built — a card that cannot change on one side without the
    other.

    `make guides` renders every element in the output ahead of the browser —
    `scripts/lib/prerender.ts` — so a property reaches a page that runs no
    script at all.

    The body is the one thing that still stands between the tags. It is the
    one thing an attribute cannot hold: out of a document it is paragraphs,
    and sometimes a list.

    The title is where TYPO3 documentation puts the target: `.. card::
    :ref:`Installation <installation>``. So the words of it are the heading and
    the reference is where the card goes. The element decides what wraps a
    title and how far the link reaches, which is over the whole card.
    `:href:` is the same thing said as a path, and wins where both stand.
#}
{#- The picture goes by the name every other directive that takes a file
    uses. An option's name belongs to the language it stands in, and
    `.. figure::` and `.. image::` already gave the file that name.

    Resolved here and not in the element. What a path means is the renderer's
    business — which document it stands in, and if it points out of the site.
    The element gets the URL that came of it. -#}
{%- set src = node.option('src') -%}
{%- set source = src ? (src is external_target ? src : asset(src)) : '' -%}
{%- set href = node.option('href') ? renderLink(node.option('href')) : linkUrl(node.link) -%}
<sds-card
    heading="{{ node.title.toString }}"
    {%- if href %} href="{{ href }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('label') %} label="{{ node.option('label') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('tag') %} tag="{{ node.option('tag') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('icon') %} icon="{{ node.option('icon') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if source %} src="{{ source }}" alt="{{ node.option('alt')|default('') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('footer') %} footer="{{ node.option('footer') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('action') %} action="{{ node.option('action') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}
>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-card>
